  "contentHtml": "\n\n                    <!-- Display video article in news article for the custom next story -->\n                    \n                    <!-- Modifying the body placing embeds,promoslots,related etc.-->\n                                        <figure><img src=\"/images/default.jpg\" alt=\"\"></figure><p><a href=\"/tag/fortis+healthcare\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Fortis Healthcare</a> on Wednesday moved the <a href=\"/tag/supreme+court\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Supreme Court</a> challenging the <a href=\"/tag/delhi+high+court\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Delhi High Court</a> judgment directing a forensic audit of transactions involving the hospital chain, Malaysia’s <a href=\"/tag/ihh+healthcare+berhad\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">IHH Healthcare Berhad</a> and <a href=\"/tag/rht+health+trust\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">RHT Health Trust</a>.In a stock exchange filing, Fortis said it filed a Special Leave Petition (SLP) before the Supreme Court on September 16 against the Delhi High Court’s August 31 judgment.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>The challenge relates to the Delhi High Court proceedings in the case titled “Daiichi Sankyo Company, Limited vs. Malvinder Mohan Singh And Ors.” and specifically to three applications covered by the court's order.</p>\n                            <p>Advt\n                            </p>\n\n                              \n                                                         \n                        <p>The Delhi High Court judgment had directed a forensic audit of transactions among <a>Fortis Healthcare</a>, IHH Healthcare and RHT Health Trust. Malaysia-based IHH holds a controlling stake in Fortis, while RHT Health Trust was floated by Fortis' former promoters <a href=\"/tag/malvinder+singh\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Malvinder Singh</a> and <a href=\"/tag/shivinder+singh\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Shivinder Singh</a>.</p><!-- PROMOSLOT_M --><p>Meanwhile, <a href=\"/tag/axis+bank\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Axis Bank</a> is also likely to move the Supreme Court later on Wednesday challenging the Delhi High Court judgment.                    </p><!-- Category Most Read Placement -->\n                                                                    \n                                                                \n                                <ul>\n                                                                            <!-- <li>By <span>Indu Bhan</span>,</li> -->\n                                    \n\n                                                                            <li>By\n                                                                                            <a>Indu Bhan</a>\n\n                                                                                                                                                                                        , \n                                                                                    </li>\n                                                                        <li><a href=\"/agency/88675387/ET-Bureau\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ET Bureau</a></li>\n                                </ul>\n                                <ul>\n                                    <!-- <li> Updated On Sep 16, 2026 at 03:22 PM IST</li> -->\n                                    <li>Published On Sep 16, 2026 at 03:22 PM IST</li>\n                                    <!-- <li class=\"desktop-view\">1 min read</li> -->\n                                </ul>\n                            \n                                        \n\n                    \n\n                    <!-- Comment Section -->\n                                            \n                                        <!-- Comment Section -->\n\n                    \n